==============================================================================
(L1)(L2) GAP-WINDOW + NO-CROSSING/NO-WRAP, checked at every run midpoint
==============================================================================
  runs sampled                        : 6264
  samples outside the three windows   : 0  -> L1 HOLDS
  runs where the ordering changed     : 0  -> L2 HOLDS

==============================================================================
(L3) RATES DISTINCT  =>  D >= 3   (the P = 1 case, PROVED)
==============================================================================
  primitive directions with a repeated rate that still have a run : 0
  -> equal rates give g_i = g_j, a zero gap, impossible in B.  D >= 3 PROVED.

==============================================================================
(L4) #RUNS EVEN  (no self-mirror run)  =>  '#runs <= 2D/3' IS 'D >= 3P'
==============================================================================
  directions with an ODD number of runs : 0
  self-mirror runs                      : 0
  -> u=0 gives g=(0,0,0) and u=1/2 gives g_i in {0,1/2}: both have a zero gap,
     so neither fixed point of u->1-u lies in B.  #runs = 2P PROVED.

==============================================================================
(L5) run <= 1/(7D) and the equality characterisation
==============================================================================
  runs violating run <= 1/(7D)          : 0  -> HOLDS
  runs attaining equality               : 900  (directions: [(1, 2, 3), (1, 2, 10), (1, 2, 17), (1, 2, 24), (1, 3, 2), (1, 9, 10), (1, 9, 17), (1, 9, 24)])
  all equality directions are (1,2,3)-orbit : False
  every equality run enters at the corner (2/7,4/7,6/7) : False

==============================================================================
(L6) LATTICE-TUBE IDENTITY:  runs <-> distinct (ordering, lattice point)
==============================================================================
  runs indexed                                   : 6264
  (ordering, lattice point) collisions           : 0  -> injective YES
  -> #runs = #{(sigma,m) : (B_sigma + m) meets the segment [0,-d]}.
     B_sigma convex => one interval each.  A LATTICE COUNT IN A THIN TUBE.

==============================================================================
(E) D >= 3P :  exhaustive proof at P<=1, and measurement above
==============================================================================
  ALL primitive triples with distinct rates <= 5 : max P = 1 at (1, 2, 3)
  (repeated rates give no runs at all, L3)  ->  D <= 5 => P <= 1  PROVED,
     i.e. the P = 2 case of D >= 3P (which needs D >= 6) is PROVED.
  primitive d in [1,30]^3 : violations of D >= 3P : 0  -> HOLDS
  max P/D = 1/3 = 0.33333 at (1, 2, 3)   (threshold 1/3 = 0.33333)
  minimal D achieving each P (the witness family):
     P=1    minimal D=3    at (1, 2, 3)        3P=3     slack 0
     P=2    minimal D=7    at (1, 6, 7)        3P=6     slack 1
     P=3    minimal D=14   at (1, 13, 14)      3P=9     slack 5
     P=4    minimal D=17   at (1, 16, 17)      3P=12    slack 5
     P=5    minimal D=21   at (1, 20, 21)      3P=15    slack 6
     P=6    minimal D=28   at (1, 27, 28)      3P=18    slack 10
